# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-M47E5.2`.
#
# `env -u ...` because a dispatch leaks its run id and home into subprocesses,
# and these tests boot their own daemons against temp homes that must see
# neither. No `ORGASMIC_ALLOW_MISSING_TOOLS` is needed: neither test wants a
# multiplexer, and the orgasmic-cli suite waives no tooling on this host.
#
# TWO tests, and they are the two that DESTROY DATA rather than the two that
# merely misreport it. Findings 1 and 3 are pinnable in-tree because each has a
# victim that can be laid down before the verb runs and looked for afterwards:
# sentinel files outside the managed root, and a worker's uncommitted output
# inside it. Finding 2 is deliberately NOT in this replay — its regression
# (`a_recovery_acquired_in_the_prune_gap_is_refused_and_the_worktree_survives`)
# reddens by *timing out* on the unfixed tree, since a prune that takes no
# daemon reservation never reaches the rendezvous to park at. A 120-second
# deadline is a real red but a poor signature, so it is left to the suite where
# it belongs rather than pinned here as if it were a message.
#
# Both filters go after `--`: `cargo test` takes exactly ONE positional
# TESTNAME, so a second one is rejected as an unexpected argument. libtest
# itself ORs any number of them.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test -p orgasmic-cli --test dispatch -- worktree_prune_refuses_a_symlinked_managed_root_and_every_sentinel_survives worktree_prune_keeps_a_worktree_whose_git_link_is_unreadable_and_names_the_reason
